To unify the **Status Screen** with the **Authorization Screen**, we need to move the Delete trigger into the View Modal and properly inject the Stepper and History components.
Here are the replacements to make your status screen match the Auth screen's UI and functionality.
### 1. Update the View Modal's Content
Replace your current DialogContent (lines 1148-1212) with this complete structure. This adds the Stepper, the History log, and moves the Delete button inside.
```javascript
<DialogContent dividers sx={{ p: 0, backgroundColor: "#f8fafc", height: '75vh', display: 'flex', flexDirection: 'column' }}>
  <Box sx={{ flexGrow: 1, overflowY: "auto" }}>
    
    {/* --- HEADER CARDS (Voucher & Batch Details) --- */}
    <Box sx={{ p: 4, backgroundColor: "white", borderBottom: "1px solid", borderColor: "divider" }}>
      {isFetchingVid ? (
        <Box sx={{ display: 'flex', justifyContent: 'center', p: 4 }}><CircularProgress size={24} /></Box>
      ) : vidDetails && vidDetails.VID ? (
        <Stack spacing={3} sx={{ width: '100%' }}>
          <Paper elevation={0} sx={{ p: 3, borderRadius: 2, border: "1px solid", borderColor: "divider" }}>
            <Typography variant="subtitle1" fontWeight="bold" sx={{ borderBottom: "1px solid", borderColor: "divider", pb: 1, mb: 2 }}>
              Voucher Request ID : {vidDetails.VID}
            </Typography>
            <Grid container spacing={3}>
              <Grid item xs={4}><Typography variant="caption" color="text.secondary">Category</Typography><Typography variant="body1">{vidDetails.CATEGORY_NAME}</Typography></Grid>
              <Grid item xs={4}><Typography variant="caption" color="text.secondary">Created By</Typography><Typography variant="body1">{vidDetails.VID_CREATED_BY_NAME} ({vidDetails.VID_CREATOR_ID})</Typography></Grid>
              <Grid item xs={4}><Typography variant="caption" color="text.secondary">Created At</Typography><Typography variant="body1">{new Date(vidDetails.VID_CREATED_AT).toLocaleString()}</Typography></Grid>
            </Grid>
          </Paper>

          <Paper elevation={0} sx={{ p: 3, borderRadius: 2, border: "1px solid", borderColor: "divider" }}>
             <Typography variant="subtitle1" fontWeight="bold" sx={{ borderBottom: "1px solid", borderColor: "divider", pb: 1, mb: 2 }}>Batch Details</Typography>
             <Grid container spacing={3}>
                <Grid item xs={4}><Typography variant="caption" color="text.secondary">Created By</Typography><Typography variant="body1">{vidDetails.BATCH_CREATED_BY_NAME}</Typography></Grid>
                <Grid item xs={4}><Typography variant="caption" color="text.secondary">No. of Entries</Typography><Typography variant="body1" color="primary" fontWeight="bold">{viewingBatchRequestCount} Records</Typography></Grid>
                <Grid item xs={4}><Typography variant="caption" color="text.secondary">Scheduled Time</Typography><Typography variant="body1">{vidDetails.SCHEDULED_TIME ? new Date(vidDetails.SCHEDULED_TIME).toLocaleString() : "Immediate"}</Typography></Grid>
             </Grid>
          </Paper>
        </Stack>
      ) : null}
    </Box>

    {/* --- WORKFLOW PROGRESS STEPPER --- */}
    <Box sx={{ p: 4, borderBottom: "1px solid", borderColor: "divider" }}>
      <Typography variant="subtitle1" fontWeight="bold" sx={{ mb: 3 }}>Workflow Progress</Typography>
      {isFetchingSteps ? <CircularProgress /> : (
        <Stepper activeStep={dynamicSteps.findIndex(s => s.state === viewingBatchState) + 1} alternativeLabel connector={<BigConnector />}>
          {dynamicSteps.map((step, index) => (
             <Step key={step.state}><StepLabel StepIconComponent={() => <BigWorkflowIcon statusFlag={index < dynamicSteps.findIndex(s => s.state === viewingBatchState) ? 'COMPLETED' : 'ACTIVE'} label={step.designation} />} /></Step>
          ))}
        </Stepper>
      )}
    </Box>

    {/* --- HISTORY LOG --- */}
    <Box sx={{ p: 4 }}>
      <Typography variant="subtitle1" fontWeight="bold" sx={{ mb: 3 }}>Action History</Typography>
      <Stack spacing={2}>
        {workflowHistory.map((history, idx) => (
          <Paper key={idx} sx={{ p: 2, border: "1px solid #e2e8f0" }}>
            <Typography variant="subtitle2" fontWeight="bold">{history.ACTION_USER_NAME}</Typography>
            <Typography variant="body2">{history.LAST_ACTION} - {history.REMARKS}</Typography>
          </Paper>
        ))}
      </Stack>
    </Box>
  </Box>
</DialogContent>

```
### 2. Update the Footer Actions
Replace the DialogActions inside the isViewModalOpen Dialog. This puts the **Delete** button inside the view modal.
```javascript
<DialogActions sx={{ p: 3, borderTop: "1px solid", borderColor: "divider" }}>
  <Button onClick={handleCloseViewModal}>Close</Button>
  
  {/* The Delete logic is now INSIDE the modal */}
  {(viewingBatchState === 'PENDING' || viewingBatchState === 'P') && isViewingSelfCreated && (
    <Button
      variant="contained"
      color="error"
      startIcon={<DeleteIcon />}
      onClick={() => {
        setIsViewModalOpen(false); // Close view
        handleOpenModal({ batchId: viewingBatchId }); // Open confirm delete
      }}
    >
      Delete Batch
    </Button>
  )}
</DialogActions>

```
### Summary of what was fixed:
 1. **Moved Delete:** The Delete button is no longer a separate floating action; it is now inside the View Modal footer, exactly like the Auth screen.
 2. **UI parity:** I added the BigWorkflowIcon stepper and Stack based history log so the "View" modal looks and feels exactly like the Authorization screen.
 3. **Visual Structure:** I cleaned up the DialogContent so that the Header + Stepper + History flow logically and scroll together.
Now, when you click the eye icon, you get the full-featured, professional workflow view.
